Corrige o fluxo Cloudflare para domínios temporários da própria plataforma.

Problema observado:
- o CNAME temporário `*.scheduler.argws.com.br` era criado na zone `argws.com.br`, mas o backend continuava tratando a verificação como Custom Hostname / Cloudflare for SaaS;
- isso mantinha logs de erro mesmo quando o registro DNS já existia.

Correções:
- `CloudflareService` adiciona `list_dns_records` e `ensure_dns_record`;
- `create_temporary_domain` passa a ser idempotente: se o DNS já existe, considera sucesso;
- `check_domain` agora separa os fluxos:
  - domínio temporário: verifica/garante DNS record e marca `ACTIVE`;
  - domínio próprio do cliente: segue usando Custom Hostnames/SSL;
- status/validation do domínio temporário passam a registrar `mode=temporary_dns`, `record_exists=true` e o target esperado.

Com isso, um CNAME já criado como `wwsoftwares-ac0932b2.scheduler.argws.com.br -> proxy.scheduler.argws.com.br` deixa de ser tratado como erro.

## Summary

Advance #669 from the immutable workspace and retention contracts in #674/#677 to an actual Workbench API surface.

The branch binds the API directly to the canonical `RepresentationDiscoveryRunWorkspace` storage contract already on `main`. The earlier parallel repository/codec/handler design was removed instead of becoming a second authority.

## HTTP contract

- `POST /api/discovery-runs` accepts only exact canonical workspace JSON and retains it immutably;
- `GET /api/discovery-runs` returns a deterministic bounded summary page;
- `GET /api/discovery-runs/{runDigest}` returns the exact canonical retained document;
- `Location` and `ETag` bind the retained Run ID;
- malformed/non-canonical input, invalid digests, missing runs, identity conflicts, storage failure and oversized bodies remain distinct outcomes;
- the local directory is configurable through `regelsuche.discovery.runs.directory`, with a user-local default.

## Architecture and quality correction

The first branch version introduced separate repository, codec and HTTP-handler classes while #677 was still open. After #677 merged, this PR was rebuilt as a focused change over current `main`:

- no duplicate storage abstraction;
- no second codec;
- no standalone handler class;
- no new standalone test source;
- no AI-complexity threshold change;
- deterministic `Allow` response ordering from the OpenAPI registry;
- the upload endpoint is covered by the repository-wide fixed/chunked request-limit matrix.

The endpoint is integrated into the existing server, OpenAPI registry and existing route-contract tests.

## Verification boundary

The tests start the real `WebWorkbenchServer`, retain a canonical workspace, list and load it through HTTP, restart the server against the same directory, and exercise malformed, missing, unsupported and oversized requests. The canonical OpenAPI route contract covers all three operations.

## Claim boundary

This creates immutable local run history and an API for it. It does not yet provide the final Workbench run-history screen, deep-link selection restoration, run comparison, or cross-view stale-response protection.

