Implements Phase 9E for #57 under master contract #1.

This source-only slice adds the first real terminal WebSocket transport boundary while deliberately keeping it inert: no PTY, no shell, no node-pty, no xterm.js and no production activation.

Security properties:
- pinned `@fastify/websocket` 11.3.0 and `@types/ws` 8.18.1 with generated lockfile;
- one default terminal runtime shares one `TerminalSessionRegistry` and one Cloudflare Access owner verifier across HTTP session mint and WebSocket claim;
- plugin is registered before routes;
- one explicit `GET /api/terminal/ws` WebSocket route; no wildcard route;
- pre-upgrade order is exact enable -> owner JWT verification -> exact production Origin -> strict Phase 9D protocol header -> atomic one-time capability claim;
- unknown/expired/revoked/replayed/malformed capabilities collapse to fixed `ADMISSION_DENIED` rather than exposing capability state;
- JWKS/verifier failure maps to fixed `AUTH_UNAVAILABLE`;
- strict `handleProtocols` negotiates only `dashboard-rpi5-terminal-v1`, never the bearer `session.<token>` entry;
- `maxPayload` is 4096 bytes and `perMessageDeflate` is disabled;
- socket handlers are attached synchronously;
- because no terminal application protocol exists yet, first client data frame revokes the session and closes with fixed 1008 policy reason; no data is echoed or executed;
- close/error cleanup revokes the claimed session;
- ordinary HTTP GET is kept out of capability admission via `request.ws` and returns fixed 426.

Official documentation reviewed before implementation: current `@fastify/websocket` repository/docs, Fastify hooks, Cloudflare Network WebSockets, and Cloudflare Access JWT validation/application-token docs.

A temporary branch-only GitHub Actions helper was used only to generate the npm lockfile reproducibly; it removed itself in the same generated-lock commit and is absent from this PR diff.

Explicitly absent: PTY allocation, `node-pty`, child process/shell spawn, xterm.js, terminal resize/input/output protocol, production env values, Cloudflare Access/Tunnel/DNS/network mutation, host/systemd/sudo/root mutation or deploy.

Closes #57 only after merge.

