`salesRawEnumRender.test.ts` imported `globSync` from `node:fs`, which wasn't introduced until Node 22 and isn't exposed in the vitest test environment, causing two test failures with `TypeError: (0 , globSync) is not a function`.

## Changes

- **`client/src/pages/salesRawEnumRender.test.ts`** — dropped the `globSync` import from `node:fs`; replaced with a small `walkSync` helper using `readdirSync` + `statSync` (universally available). Produces identical results to the original `**/*.{ts,tsx}` glob pattern with no new dependencies.

```ts
// Before
import { globSync } from "node:fs";
const files = globSync("**/*.{ts,tsx}", { cwd: CLIENT_SRC })
  .filter(...)
  .map((f) => join(CLIENT_SRC, f));

// After
function walkSync(dir: string, ext: RegExp, results: string[] = []): string[] {
  for (const entry of readdirSync(dir)) {
    const full = join(dir, entry);
    if (statSync(full).isDirectory()) walkSync(full, ext, results);
    else if (ext.test(entry)) results.push(full);
  }
  return results;
}
const files = walkSync(CLIENT_SRC, /\.(ts|tsx)$/).filter(...);
```

